From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] K3: close audit findings — RHCT ISA, _OSC masks, hart contract, IDs, GMAC rows, clock semantics

K3: close audit findings — RHCT ISA, _OSC masks, hart contract, IDs, GMAC rows, clock semantics

- RHCT: complete the X100 ISA string from K3Cpus.dtsi. Under ACPI the
  kernel does NOT imply zicsr/zifencei/zicntr/zihpm from base letters
  (unlike DT), so every implemented extension is now listed: adds
  zicntr zicond zicsr zifencei zihintpause zihpm zfh zfhmin zba zbb
  zbc zbs zkt zvbb..zvkt (vector-crypto) svinval svnapot. Missing
  names silently dropped HWCAP/perf capability. (Audit item 5)
- _OSC (PCI0): Support (CDW2) and Control (CDW3) are DIFFERENT
  bitfields with different bit assignments. Support confirms MSI
  (0x10 in CDW2: the APLIC-MSI + IMSIC path is live). Control grants
  only PCIeCapability (0x10 in CDW3: MCFG ECAM); hot-plug/SHPC/PME/
  AER/LTR/DPC have no firmware backing (no _PRT, no GPE wiring). The
  earlier CTRL=CDW3&SUPP mixed the fields - the two 0x10 values are
  different bits that happen to coincide. (Item 8)
- Hart contract: ACPI describes ONLY the 8 X100 harts. Documented at
  PcdX100HartCount; unused PcdHartCount dropped from the tables INF.
  (Item 3)
- ACPI ID provenance: USB2 808622B7 (Intel BSW DWC3) and DBI0
  AMZN0001 (Amazon Annapurna) are BORROWED IDs - documented in AML
  with the proper fix gated on a qualified boot. (Item 10)
- DBI0 _CRS: ResourceProducer -> ResourceConsumer. (Item 11)
- ClockDxe: GMAC1/2 TX/PHY rows retargeted to their own EMAC blocks.
  (Item 9)
- EnableClock: zero-address rows fail with EFI_DEVICE_ERROR. (Item 12)
- ResetSystemLib: deadloop documented terminal by design. (Item 13)

Verified: full RELEASE build clean; built AML decodes the PCI _OSC
with separate CDW2&0x10 / CDW3&0x10 masks and DBI0 ResourceConsumer;
RHCT carries the complete string. Hardware re-validation pending.
---
diff --git a/Platform/Spacemit/K3/AcpiTables/Dsdt/Dsdt.asl b/Platform/Spacemit/K3/AcpiTables/Dsdt/Dsdt.asl
index f069dc60..d38b6c6c 100644
--- a/Platform/Spacemit/K3/AcpiTables/Dsdt/Dsdt.asl
+++ b/Platform/Spacemit/K3/AcpiTables/Dsdt/Dsdt.asl
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ DefinitionBlock ("DsdtTable.aml", "DSDT", 2, "SPMT  ", "K3", EFI_ACPI_OEM_REVISI
   include ("Cpu.asl")
 
   Scope (_SB) {
+
     Device (IC00)
     {
       Name (_HID, "RSCV0002")
@@ -118,6 +119,14 @@ DefinitionBlock ("DsdtTable.aml", "DSDT", 2, "SPMT  ", "K3", EFI_ACPI_OEM_REVISI
 
     Device (USB2)
     {
+      /*
+       * BORROWED ACPI ID: "808622B7" is Intel Braswell DWC3. The dwc3
+       * core driver matches it (ACPI_ID_INTEL_BSW) and the K3 DWC3 is
+       * register-compatible, but this ID is not SpacemiT's and implies
+       * Intel-specific quirks in future kernels. Proper fix: PRP0001 +
+       * compatible "snps,dwc3" (the core also matches by compatible);
+       * requires a qualified boot before switching. Linux-only binding.
+       */
       Name (_HID, "808622B7")
       Name (_UID, Zero)
       Name (_CCA, 0)
@@ -203,11 +212,17 @@ DefinitionBlock ("DsdtTable.aml", "DSDT", 2, "SPMT  ", "K3", EFI_ACPI_OEM_REVISI
           CreateDWordField (Arg3, 4, CDW2)
           CreateDWordField (Arg3, 8, CDW3)
 
-          SUPP = CDW2
-          CTRL = CDW3
-
-          /* Allow: PCIeHotPlug SHPCHotPlug PME AER PCIeCapability */
-          CTRL &= 0x1F
+          /*
+           * Support (CDW2) and Control (CDW3) are DIFFERENT bitfields
+           * with different bit assignments - they must not be mixed.
+           * Support: MSI (0x10) is provided (the APLIC-MSI path and the
+           * IMSIC MSI domain are live). Control: only the PCIe
+           * Capability bit (0x10 in CDW3: extended config via MCFG) is
+           * granted; hot-plug, SHPC, PME, AER, LTR, DPC have no firmware
+           * backing (no _PRT, no GPE wiring, no AER handler).
+           */
+          SUPP = CDW2 & 0x10
+          CTRL = CDW3 & 0x10
 
           If (Arg1 != 1) { CDW1 |= 0x08 } /* unknown revision */
           If (CDW3 != CTRL) { CDW1 |= 0x10 } /* capabilities lost */
@@ -239,12 +254,21 @@ DefinitionBlock ("DsdtTable.aml", "DSDT", 2, "SPMT  ", "K3", EFI_ACPI_OEM_REVISI
       // PCIe host bridge 0 DBI registers (reserve from generic use).
       Device (DBI0)
       {
-        Name (_HID, "AMZN0001")
+        /*
+     * BORROWED ACPI ID: "AMZN0001" is Amazon Annapurna Labs PCIe DBI
+     * (acpi_get_rc_resources in pcie-al.c). The K3 DBI window is
+     * register-space only and nothing on this kernel binds it, but the
+     * ID is not SpacemiT's and could bind pcie-al on other kernels.
+     * Proper fix: PRP0001 + a documented compatible, or drop _HID for a
+     * pure PNP0C02-style reservation; requires a qualified boot.
+     * Linux-only consideration.
+     */
+    Name (_HID, "AMZN0001")
         Name (_CID, "PNP0C02")
         Name (_UID, 0)
         Name (_CRS, ResourceTemplate () {
           QWordMemory (
-            ResourceProducer, PosDecode, MinFixed, MaxFixed,
+            ResourceConsumer, PosDecode, MinFixed, MaxFixed,
             NonCacheable, ReadWrite,
             0x0,           // AddressGranularity
             0x80000000,    // AddressMinimum (DBI)
